{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Analysis record (no code change). Measured gate economics 2026-08-03→08-11 from attested sidecars + usage logs; brainstormed and evaluated cost levers against history, OSS/academic research, and $52.70 of Bedrock experiments. Deliverables: reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/ (README + full HTML report + experiment arm outputs) and artifact https://claude.ai/code/artifact/a59a29df-f641-4c3f-b7b0-c6333314935f. Headline: plan-review $3.02/run (median $2.27), code-review $1.42/run, completion $2.24/run; $11.85 mean per ticket completed (2.1 plan + ~1.75 code + 1.2 completion runs); ~20% of spend on terminally-failed calls (overlap-judge 48k output overruns; completion-verifier ~190-request loop deaths). Top levers: fix the two failure pathologies (~15-20%, zero quality risk); ship the unshipped 696a AGENT→1-TURN demotion via ADR-0054 replay (15-30%); per-criterion incremental re-review (15-25%, moderate risk); Nova pilot for single-turn ops (Nova Pro 29/30 gold, Nova 2 Lite 27/28 with zero gold-regressing flips vs committed Opus/Sonnet arms). Refuted: Haiku for agentic ops (5 false-accepts + loop runaway → cost 6x Nova Pro); Sonnet-for-code-review (2 gold-regressing over-blocks).","id":"b902-18af-14ed-4da1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"LLM gate cost analysis since Bedrock switch: per-run/per-ticket costs, lever option book, cheap-model experiments (2026-08-11)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786426084120149001,"uuid":"cf857966-1a39-4f0a-be5e-5d8dbfcb562a"}